<!-- ===================== STAGE 1: ONBOARDING ===================== -->
<section class="section" id="onboarding">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
    <div class="portal-stage-header">
      <span class="portal-stage-tag">Stage 1 &middot; New clients</span>
      <h2>Onboarding intake.</h2>
      <p>This is the form we send after the discovery call. The more detail you give us up front, the faster we launch. Usually 3 to 4 weeks of build time once it comes back. You can save what you have and return later; nothing has to be filled out in one sitting.</p>

      <div class="portal-stage-meta">
        <div>
          <strong>Typical time</strong>
          15&ndash;25 minutes
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>What happens next</strong>
          We schedule a 30-minute follow-up to fill any gaps and align on timeline.
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Privacy</strong>
          Confidential, never shared. <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="inline-link">Privacy policy</a>.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <a href="/onboarding/" class="portal-card portal-card--feature">
      <span class="portal-icon">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="9" y1="13" x2="15" y2="13"/><line x1="9" y1="17" x2="15" y2="17"/></svg>
      </span>
      <h3>Open the onboarding form</h3>
      <p>Nine sections covering your business, services, customers, brand, and assets. Submit whatever you have ready; come back later for the rest. Anything you can't put in writing, we'll cover on the follow-up call.</p>
      <span class="portal-arrow">Start the intake &rarr;</span>
    </a>

    <p style="margin-top:2rem;font-size:0.92rem;color:var(--text-muted);text-align:center">Prefer to send this some other way? Email a Google Doc, Dropbox Paper, or Notion page to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.email }}</a>. Same place either way.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== STAGE 2: IN BUILD ===================== -->
<section class="section section--cream" id="in-build">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:980px">
    <div class="portal-stage-header">
      <span class="portal-stage-tag">Stage 2 &middot; In active build</span>
      <h2>Reviewing your preview link.</h2>
      <p>Once your design is in our hands, we'll send a private preview URL. The form below is how you give us structured feedback: what's working, what to change, what to question. Unlimited revision rounds; honest notes always beat polite ones.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="portal-grid portal-grid--two">
      <a href="/design-feedback/" class="portal-card">
        <span class="portal-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="13.5" cy="6.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"/><path d="M12 2a10 10 0 0 0 0 20 3 3 0 0 0 3-3 2.5 2.5 0 0 1 2.5-2.5H19a3 3 0 0 0 3-3A10 10 0 0 0 12 2z"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Design feedback</h3>
        <p>Structured notes get us to the right revisions faster. Drop the preview URL, tell us what's working and what isn't, and how urgent the changes are.</p>
        <span class="portal-arrow">Give feedback &rarr;</span>
      </a>

      <div class="portal-card portal-card--info">
        <span class="portal-icon portal-icon--info">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>How feedback rounds work</h3>
        <ul class="portal-bullets">
          <li>Round 1: design preview &rarr; your feedback &rarr; revisions in 2&ndash;3 business days</li>
          <li>Round 2: refined preview &rarr; targeted notes &rarr; usually one more pass</li>
          <li>Round 3+: rare; we usually nail it by round 2 with good notes</li>
          <li>Final approval: you sign off, we ship to staging for content load</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== STAGE 3: LIVE ===================== -->
<section class="section" id="live">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:980px">
    <div class="portal-stage-header">
      <span class="portal-stage-tag">Stage 3 &middot; Site is live</span>
      <h2>Day-to-day requests.</h2>
      <p>Once your site is live, three forms cover most of what you'll need. Use the urgency cue at the top of each; emergency goes through a different channel than a routine update.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="portal-grid">
      <a href="/content-update/" class="portal-card">
        <span class="portal-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.12 2.12 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4L16.5 3.5z"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Content update</h3>
        <p>New hours, new service, photo swap, typo fix, price change, seasonal callout. Usually live the same business day.</p>
        <span class="portal-arrow">Submit a change &rarr;</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/emergency/" class="portal-card portal-card--urgent">
        <span class="portal-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Emergency support</h3>
        <p>Site down, wrong info live, security concern, billing issue showing. Triaged immediately, usually within the hour during business hours.</p>
        <span class="portal-arrow">Report an emergency &rarr;</span>
      </a>

      <div class="portal-card portal-card--info">
        <span class="portal-icon portal-icon--info">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>What "emergency" means</h3>
        <ul class="portal-bullets">
          <li>Your site is fully down or returning errors to visitors</li>
          <li>Wrong contact info live and customers are calling the wrong number</li>
          <li>You see a defaced page, suspicious form submissions, or any security concern</li>
          <li>A new product / promo is live with the wrong price</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin:0.85rem 0 0">Anything else (new service page, photo swap, copy change) goes through the content-update form. We get to those same business day.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="portal-quick-row">
      <strong>Truly time-critical?</strong>
      <span>Don't wait for the form. Call or text <a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" class="inline-link">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>. We pick up or call back fast.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

